From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: describe the ADSP sleepstate SMP2P entry

The SM8750 vendor devicetree adds a "sleepstate" outbound entry to the
ADSP SMP2P edge and a qcom,smp2p-sleepstate node that uses bit 12 of it
to tell the ADSP whether the application processor is awake. Describe
both, disabled: an enabled entry without the driver would read as the
AP being asleep. Boards that want the notification enable them.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -608,6 +608,20 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 		};
+
+		smp2p_sleepstate_out: sleepstate-out {
+			qcom,entry-name = "sleepstate";
+			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+	};
+
+	/* Bit 12 of the ADSP "sleepstate" entry reports the AP as awake */
+	smp2p_sleepstate: smp2p-sleepstate {
+		compatible = "qcom,smp2p-sleepstate";
+		qcom,smem-states = <&smp2p_sleepstate_out 12>;
+		qcom,smem-state-names = "awake";
+		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
 	smp2p-cdsp {
